# Spec Authoring

Produce one reproducible Markdown specification from section sources and figures.

1. Confirm the authorized destination, specification scope, requirements and
   revision. Require Python >=3.11, uv and Graphviz `dot`; missing tools return
   `TOOL_MISSING`. Scan new acquisitions with scan-software-supply-chain first.
2. Copy this skill's `template/` to the destination without overwriting existing
   work. Fill `spec.yaml` title, document_id and revision history.
3. Author the numbered sections using [section rules](references/section-rules.md).
   Keep the floor subsections; cite requirements-engineering for statement
   quality instead of inventing a second checklist. Unresolved intent returns
   `NEEDS_OWNER_DECISION`; placeholders remain visible gaps, never acceptance.
4. Author figure YAML using [figure rules](references/figures.md). Set `kit` to
   this skill's `scripts/` (or the vendored directory), then run:
   `uv run --script "$kit/diagram.py" render <figure.yaml>`.
   Commit YAML, SVG and draw.io together; edit YAML, never generated outputs.
5. Run `uv run --script "$kit/spec_build.py" <spec-dir> <output.md>`,
   `uv run --script "$kit/spec_lint.py" <spec-dir>` and
   `uv run --script "$kit/diagram.py" lint <spec-dir>`.
   Build generates front matter, numbering and Appendix A. Never edit the build.
6. Build again to a temporary output and compare bytes with `cmp`. In a git
   worktree also use `git diff --exit-code -- <output.md>` when checking an
   already committed build for staleness. Outside git, byte comparison suffices.
7. Correct source findings and rerun affected commands, at most three rounds
   with new evidence each time. Stop on no new evidence or missing tools;
   never weaken rules to hide findings. See [vendoring](references/vendoring.md)
   only when another repository needs its own CI-accessible tool copy.
8. Return `SUCCESS` only for zero findings and identical rebuilds, with source
   paths, output, command exits and unresolved content gaps. Otherwise return
   `VALIDATION_FAILED`, `TOOL_MISSING` or `NEEDS_OWNER_DECISION` with the blocker.
   Mechanical success is not formal review, acceptance or publication authority.
